From c2314a30025e2dbe24577293ed0cc93370f70a42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tesseract XRT port <jwkim@limagin.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:23:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] libxdma, libqdma: avoid empty if/else bodies
 (-Wempty-body)

With -Wextra on by default since v6.10 (mainline commit f5982cceb347),
gcc reports "suggest braces around empty body" for:
 - four "if (...) dbg_init(...);" / "else dbg_init(...);" statements in
   lib/libxdma.c, because the disabled dbg_init() expands to nothing;
 - a literal "if (detail) ;" in libqdma's qdma_kthread_dump().

Make the disabled dbg_init() expand to "do { } while (0)" (the usual
kernel form for a no-op statement macro; the enabled form is pr_err and
is unchanged), and drop the empty if statement, whose condition is a
plain int parameter without side effects.

Guard: none needed; both forms are valid on every compiler and kernel.

Equivalence: exact; both edits replace an empty statement with an
empty statement.

Upstream: not addressed in XRT master or in the libqdma version it
pins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SpY5QiU1d7kAe8YJM35EvA
---
 .../xocl/lib/libqdma/QDMA/linux-kernel/driver/libqdma/thread.c | 3 ---
 driver/xocl/lib/libxdma.h                                      | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/driver/xocl/lib/libqdma/QDMA/linux-kernel/driver/libqdma/thread.c b/driver/xocl/lib/libqdma/QDMA/linux-kernel/driver/libqdma/thread.c
index d0c0909..b45aa42 100644
--- a/driver/xocl/lib/libqdma/QDMA/linux-kernel/driver/libqdma/thread.c
+++ b/driver/xocl/lib/libqdma/QDMA/linux-kernel/driver/libqdma/thread.c
@@ -38,9 +38,6 @@ int qdma_kthread_dump(struct qdma_kthread *thp, char *buf, int buflen,
 	len += snprintf(buf, buflen, "%s, cpu %u, work %u.\n",
 			thp->name, thp->cpu, thp->work_cnt);
 
-	if (detail)
-		;
-
 	unlock_thread(thp);
 
 	buf[len] = '\0';
diff --git a/driver/xocl/lib/libxdma.h b/driver/xocl/lib/libxdma.h
index 87d1a21..8e148cd 100644
--- a/driver/xocl/lib/libxdma.h
+++ b/driver/xocl/lib/libxdma.h
@@ -246,7 +246,7 @@
 #define dbg_sg(...)
 #define dbg_tfr(...)
 #define dbg_irq(...)
-#define dbg_init(...)
+#define dbg_init(...)	do { } while (0)
 #define dbg_desc(...)
 #endif
 
